WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.100
Messages claiming to be from HMRC, your bank, Royal Mail or a parcel company, with a link and pressure to act: «your account will be blocked», «pay a fee».

2
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:28.200
Your bank will never ask for your PIN or your full password, or ask you to move money to a «safe account». Forward suspicious texts free to 7726 and emails to report@phishing.gov.uk.

3
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:37.700
If someone calls claiming to be your bank, hang up and dial 159: it connects you to your bank safely.

4
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:50.300
If you have lost money in England or Wales, call your bank straight away and report it to Report Fraud (0300 123 2040). In Scotland, to Police Scotland.

5
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.600
Say it aloud: “I didn't make this payment.”.
